{"id":"FIG-f48bbeddce8c8a0c","src":"figure","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE","page":70,"text":"","caption":"Figure 4.17: This ﬁgure illustrates the activation of a runnable without minimum start interval. The started state of the runnable main states and the activated state of the runnable activation states are shown. Each ﬂash indicates the occurrence of an RTE event. The runnable can only be activated once. The activation is not queued. The runnable can be activated again when it is still started.","sha":"f48bbeddce8c8a0ce663baf20866d7ed98f1418d5b5668092a6d1ea609d1ebf0","series":[{"id":"FIG-f48bbeddce8c8a0c","releases":["R2.1.20","R3.0.7","R3.1.5","R3.2.3"],"sha":"f48bbeddce8c8a0ce663baf20866d7ed98f1418d5b5668092a6d1ea609d1ebf0"}],"releases":["R2.1.20","R3.0.7","R3.1.5","R3.2.3"],"occurrences":[{"release":"R2.1.20","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE","page":66,"pdf":"R2.1.20/AUTOSAR/CLASSIC/AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE.pdf"},{"release":"R3.0.7","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE","page":70,"pdf":"R3.0.7/AUTOSAR/CLASSIC/AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE.pdf"},{"release":"R3.1.5","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE","page":70,"pdf":"R3.1.5/AUTOSAR/CLASSIC/AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE.pdf"}],"kind":"figure","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Runnable minimum start interval semantics","rel":[],"id":"TPS_SWCT_01302"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.8,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Constraint on minimumStartInterval and concurrency","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Rte_02733"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.75,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"RTE event activation vector provision","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Rte_08055"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.7,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Inter-runnable triggering minimum start interval","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Rte_07224"}],"ok":true,"schema":"versions-explorer@1"}